 ## Background
-The method originates from GPU Pro 3, specifically the chapter on voxelization via rendering [S1, unofficial]. It is designed to bridge the gap between continuous world coordinates and discrete voxel indices, enabling efficient rasterization of geometry into a voxel buffer. The approach is widely used in real-time volume rendering and voxel-based collision detection systems.
